node_modules/
dist/

# THE REPLAY VIEWER IS NOT COMMITTED. It is a build artifact of the cartridge, and it now comes from
# the cartridge's own artifact image -- `COPY --from=ants` in the Dockerfile, and
# scripts/vendor-viewers.sh (via `predev`/`prebuild`) for the local Vite loop.
#
# It used to be committed, because this image's build context is web/ alone and could not reach a
# sibling checkout of ants. The cost was that `npm run dev` silently rewrote checked-in files from
# whatever sibling happened to be there. Now the same script writes only ignored files, from a named
# image, so running it is inert.
public/cartridges/

# TypeScript incremental build info
*.tsbuildinfo

# Vite
.vite/
vite.config.ts.timestamp-*

